* Helm is a package manager for Kubernetes that helps you manage Kubernetes applications using Charts (preconfigured resources). 

Below is a list of commonly used Helm commands

     Command	                                 Description
helm version	                         Show the version of Helm
helm help	                         List all available Helm commands
helm repo add <name> <url>	         Add a Helm chart repository
helm repo update	                 Update info about available charts
helm search hub <keyword>	         Search Helm Hub for charts
helm search repo <keyword>	         Search your added repositories
helm install <release-name> <chart>	 Install a chart
helm upgrade <release-name> <chart>	 Upgrade a release
helm uninstall <release-name>	         Uninstall a release
helm list	                         List releases
helm status <release-name>	         Get the status of a release
helm get all <release-name>	         Get all info about a release
helm show values <chart>	         Show default values of a chart
helm template <chart>	                 Render templates locally
helm lint <chart>	                 Check chart for issues

Working with Chart Values

     Command	                                                 Description
helm install -f values.yaml <release-name> <chart>	Install a chart with custom values
helm upgrade -f values.yaml <release-name> <chart>	Upgrade using custom values
helm get values <release-name>	                        Get the values of a release
helm diff upgrade <release-name> <chart> (with plugin)	See what will change before upgrading

Chart Management

      Command	                                Description
helm create <chart-name>	        Create a new chart 
helm package <chart>	                Package a chart directory
helm dependency update <chart-dir>	Update dependencies
helm dependency build <chart-dir>	Build chart dependencies



